# Example Tactical Data Link (XTDL) — a FICTIONAL binary format invented only to
# show the overlay shape. It is not a real standard and encodes nothing real.
# One 6-byte word, LSB-first bit ranges, decoded through the public `bits` wire.
# Marked `controlled` to show the mechanics: it uses the public `core` module
# (so it converts to every public format) and the overlay's own `xtdl` module
# (so it carries `xtdl.sector` to other formats that also use that module).
format     xtdl-example
version    0.2.0
distribution controlled
source     "invented for this example; no external document"
wire       bits
word_bytes 6
uses       xtdl
field  lat          0:0:21    linscale:1048575:90
field  lon          0:21:22   linscale:2097151:180
field  xtdl.sector  0:43:5    uint
